#sleela 1.9
// A newer MINOR within the same MAJOR. Per SL-META-0001 Section 4.4, MINOR
// increments only ADD constructs, so a 1.0-syntax program is forward-declarable
// as 1.9 only if the compiler supports 1.9. With max supported = 1.0 this file
// is still "too new" and MUST be rejected -- proving MINOR is enforced too.
class MinorAhead {
    void main() {
        print("unreachable on a 1.0 compiler");
    }
}
